### Real-World Example 1: Provider Credentialing Background Checks

**Context**: Gainwell Provider+™ portal enables healthcare providers to submit credentialing applications for enrollment in state Medicaid programs. The credentialing workflow includes background checks with external agencies (NPPES NPI registry verification, state medical board licensure verification, OIG exclusion list screening, SAM.gov federal debarment checks) that typically take 2-3 minutes per provider to complete. Under synchronous processing, these operations frequently exceeded API gateway timeouts (60 seconds), causing credentialing applications to fail mid-process and forcing providers to resubmit applications.

**Problem Scope**: During annual provider re-credentialing period, 200+ concurrent credentialing applications created thread pool exhaustion, causing 4-hour system-wide outage affecting all provider portal functionality. Post-incident analysis showed:
- Thread pool exhaustion at 50 concurrent long-running operations (2-3 minutes each)
- 40% of credentialing requests failed with HTTP 504 Gateway Timeout errors
- 150+ provider support tickets monthly from timeout-related application failures
- Estimated $340K annual lost productivity from providers unable to submit claims during credentialing delays
- State contract SLA risk: 24-hour credentialing turnaround time not achievable with synchronous processing

**Implementation**:

1. **API Endpoint Changes**: Converted `POST /api/providers/credentialing/submit` from synchronous to asynchronous:
   ```csharp
   // BEFORE (Synchronous - Problematic)
   [HttpPost("submit")]
   public async Task<IActionResult> SubmitCredentialingApplication(
       [FromBody] CredentialingApplication application)
   {
       // Validate application (200ms)
       await ValidateApplication(application);

       // Perform background checks synchronously (2-3 minutes) - BLOCKS REQUEST
       var nppesResult = await VerifyNPPESRegistry(application.NPI);
       var licenseResult = await VerifyStateLicense(application.StateLicenseNumber);
       var oigResult = await CheckOIGExclusionList(application.NPI);
       var samResult = await CheckSAMDebarment(application.TaxId);

       // Save results and return (500ms)
       await SaveCredentialingResults(application.Id, nppesResult,
           licenseResult, oigResult, samResult);

       return Ok(new { status = "Approved", credentialingId = application.Id });
       // Total time: 2-3 minutes, frequently times out
   }

   // AFTER (Asynchronous - Solution)
   [HttpPost("submit")]
   public async Task<IActionResult> SubmitCredentialingApplication(
       [FromBody] CredentialingApplication application)
   {
       // Validate application (200ms)
       await ValidateApplication(application);

       // Create credentialing job (50ms)
       var job = await _jobService.CreateJobAsync(
           tenantId: GetTenantId(),
           jobType: "ProviderCredentialing",
           userId: GetUserId(),
           parameters: new Dictionary<string, object>
           {
               ["applicationId"] = application.Id,
               ["npi"] = application.NPI,
               ["stateLicenseNumber"] = application.StateLicenseNumber,
               ["taxId"] = application.TaxId
           });

       // Enqueue job for background processing (50ms)
       await _jobQueue.EnqueueAsync(job);

       // Return immediately with job tracking ID (total: <300ms)
       return StatusCode(StatusCodes.Status202Accepted, new
       {
           message = "Credentialing application submitted successfully. Background checks in progress.",
           jobId = job.Id,
           statusUrl = Url.Action("GetJobStatus", "Jobs", new { jobId = job.Id }),
           estimatedCompletionMinutes = 3
       });
   }
   ```

2. **Background Worker Implementation**: Created Azure Function worker processing credentialing background checks:
   ```csharp
   [Function("ProviderCredentialingWorker")]
   public async Task ProcessCredentialingJob(
       [ServiceBusTrigger("job-processing", "credentialing-subscription")]
       ServiceBusReceivedMessage message)
   {
       var jobData = JsonSerializer.Deserialize<JobMessage>(message.Body);

       await _jobService.UpdateJobStatusAsync(jobData.JobId, JobStatus.Running);

       try
       {
           // Perform background checks with progress updates
           await _jobService.UpdateJobProgressAsync(jobData.JobId, 25);
           var nppesResult = await VerifyNPPESRegistry(jobData.Parameters["npi"]);

           await _jobService.UpdateJobProgressAsync(jobData.JobId, 50);
           var licenseResult = await VerifyStateLicense(jobData.Parameters["stateLicenseNumber"]);

           await _jobService.UpdateJobProgressAsync(jobData.JobId, 75);
           var oigResult = await CheckOIGExclusionList(jobData.Parameters["npi"]);
           var samResult = await CheckSAMDebarment(jobData.Parameters["taxId"]);

           // Save results
           var credentialingStatus = DetermineCredentialingStatus(
               nppesResult, licenseResult, oigResult, samResult);

           await _jobService.CompleteJobAsync(jobData.JobId, new Dictionary<string, object>
           {
               ["credentialingStatus"] = credentialingStatus,
               ["nppesVerified"] = nppesResult.IsVerified,
               ["licenseVerified"] = licenseResult.IsValid,
               ["oigClear"] = !oigResult.IsExcluded,
               ["samClear"] = !samResult.IsDebarred
           });

           // Send webhook notification to provider portal
           await SendCredentialingCompletionWebhook(jobData.Parameters["applicationId"], credentialingStatus);
       }
       catch (Exception ex)
       {
           await _jobService.FailJobAsync(jobData.JobId, ex.Message, ex.StackTrace);
       }
   }
   ```

3. **UI Changes**: Updated provider portal to show progress indicator and enable navigation away from credentialing submission:
   ```typescript
